{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KTAYFqfYT9mywyEz69aoin","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Extracted ceo-boot declarations executed by the facade.\"\"\"\n2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n3\t\n4\t\n5\t\n6\t# PLAN-177 t2 (re-pass rc.4 P1-f). The POSITIVE half of the probe test.\n7\t#\n8\t# The S303 filter below identified a probe by ABSENCE alone — five governed\n9\t# markers missing — and absence is the shape of the events the ratio exists to\n10\t# find: a markerless real spawn (including one the PreToolUse hook admitted by\n11\t# failing open) was classified as harness noise and removed from the\n12\t# denominator. A probe-only window then reported green with\n13\t# `harness_probes_skipped=1` while the governance gap it was built to surface\n14\t# went unrendered.\n15\t#\n16\t# So the structural conditions are necessary, not sufficient: the row must ALSO\n17\t# carry the observed harness signature. The signature is CLOSED — the literal\n18\t# description the tool-materialization probe emits, anchored at both ends\n19\t# (`Load <Tool> via ToolSearch?`, S303 observation, prompt `noop`) — plus\n20\t# corroboration by `desc_hash`, which the emitter computes over the RAW\n21\t# description: if the two disagree the preview was truncated or redacted, i.e.\n22\t# not this short, secret-free probe line. Anything else counts. Every\n23\t# uncertainty resolves toward VISIBLE.\n24\t_HARNESS_PROBE_DESC_RE = re.compile(\n25\t    r\"\\ALoad [A-Za-z0-9_.\\-]+(?:,[ ]?[A-Za-z0-9_.\\-]+)* via ToolSearch\\?\\Z\"\n26\t)\n27\t\n28\t\n29\tdef _has_harness_probe_fingerprint(ev: Dict[str, Any]) -> bool:\n30\t    \"\"\"True iff the row carries the CLOSED, observed harness-probe signature.\n31\t\n32\t    Positive identification, never inferred from missing fields. An absent or\n33\t    non-matching `desc_hash` is NOT corroboration, so it returns False and the\n34\t    row is counted — the safe direction for an advisory that exists to expose\n35\t    unclassified spawns.\n36\t    \"\"\"\n37\t    desc = ev.get(\"desc_preview\")\n38\t    if not isinstance(desc, str) or not _HARNESS_PROBE_DESC_RE.match(desc):\n39\t        return False\n40\t    digest = ev.get(\"desc_hash\")\n41\t    if not isinstance(digest, str) or not digest:\n42\t        return False\n43\t    return digest == hashlib.sha256(desc.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n44\t\n45\t\n46\tdef _is_harness_probe_event(ev: Dict[str, Any]) -> bool:\n47\t    \"\"\"True iff the agent_spawn row is a harness-internal tool-loading probe.\n48\t\n49\t    S303: the ghost filter above was written for the ToolSearch probes of an\n50\t    older harness, whose Agent-shaped PostToolUse rows carried NO description\n51\t    (desc_preview == \"\" and desc_hash == SHA256(b\"\")). The current harness\n52\t    supplies a human-readable description for the same class of call — e.g.\n53\t    ``Load WebFetch via ToolSearch?`` with prompt ``noop`` and a fixed cheap\n54\t    model — so all four ghost conditions no longer hold and a pure\n55\t    tool-materialization probe lands in the denominator as a governance gap.\n56\t\n57\t    The discriminator is ``subagent_type``: the Agent/Task spawn contract makes\n58\t    it REQUIRED for every governed dispatch (``check_agent_spawn.py`` derives\n59\t    the authoritative archetype from it, and ``extract_skill`` Path D needs it),\n60\t    so a row that carries none was never a CEO dispatch. All five conditions\n61\t    must hold — no subagent_type, no archetype, no rail attribution, no\n62\t    ``## AGENT PROFILE`` and no ``## FILE ASSIGNMENT`` — so a real named spawn\n63\t    that merely lost one field still counts.\n64\t\n65\t    T-2 STATUS (re-pass rc.4 t5/t7 P2): DEFERRED, not cured — this function\n66\t    ALWAYS returns False today and probe-shaped rows COUNT in the\n67\t    denominator (a probe-only window reads 1/1 red and the operator\n68\t    triages it). The former ``harness_probes_skipped`` counter was removed\n69\t    together with the exemption; no row is skipped, so nothing is\n70\t    \"reported through\" anything.\n71\t\n72\t    PLAN-177 t2 (P1-f): those five are NECESSARY, NOT SUFFICIENT. Absence is\n73\t    exactly the shape of the event this ratio exists to expose — a markerless\n74\t    REAL spawn, including one admitted because the PreToolUse hook failed\n75\t    open, matched all five and was deleted from the denominator. The row must\n76\t    ALSO carry the closed harness signature\n77\t    (``_has_harness_probe_fingerprint``); an unrecognised description counts,\n78\t    however markerless the row is.\n79\t    \"\"\"\n80\t    # Re-pass rc.4 t2 (P1): the S303 exemption is RETIRED until trusted\n81\t    # provenance exists. `desc_preview` and `desc_hash` are both derived\n82\t    # from the same CALLER-CONTROLLED description, so the hash corroborates\n83\t    # nothing: a real markerless spawn described as\n84\t    # `Load WebFetch via ToolSearch?` was silently deleted from the\n85\t    # denominator — the exact event this ratio exists to expose. Until the\n86\t    # EMITTER can stamp provenance the caller cannot forge, probe-shaped\n87\t    # rows COUNT (the conservative direction for an advisory: a yellow the\n88\t    # operator triages beats a green that hides a fail-open spawn).\n89\t    # _has_harness_probe_fingerprint is kept (tested) as the shape\n90\t    # DETECTOR for that future provenance-bearing emitter.\n91\t    return False\n92\t\n93\t\n94\tdef check_skill_unknown_ratio() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n95\t    \"\"\"Detect spawns that should have SKILL injection but didn't.\n96\t\n97\t    S94 follow-up: excludes intentionally skill-less archetypes —\n98\t    `general-purpose` subagent dispatches via the mitigated rail\n99\t    (ADR-082) by design have no SKILL.md anchor. They broker cross-\n100\t    LLM gate calls and similar utility work; counting them as FPs\n101\t    inflates the ratio to 100% during healthy Codex MCP sessions\n102\t    and trains the operator to ignore the channel.\n103\t\n104\t    A spawn counts as \"skill missing\" ONLY when its `archetype` is\n105\t    a custom (non-general-purpose) one AND `skill` is unknown/empty.\n106\t    That is the original PLAN-020 ADR-051 governance gap the\n107\t    detector was built for.\n108\t    \"\"\"\n109\t    # T-2 STATUS (re-pass rc.4 t5 P2): DEFERRED, not cured. Both the S86\n110\t    # ghost filter and the S303 probe filter are RETIRED (absence-based,\n111\t    # caller-forgeable); every agent_spawn row counts until the EMITTER can\n112\t    # stamp provenance the caller cannot forge. The skipped counters were\n113\t    # removed with them — a permanently-zero counter reads as \"filter\n114\t    # active, nothing skipped\", which is the wrong claim.\n115\t    total = 0\n116\t    unknown = 0\n117\t    skill_less_by_design = 0\n118\t    test_pollution_skipped = 0\n119\t    for ev in _iter_audit_events_since(24):\n120\t        if ev.get(\"action\") != \"agent_spawn\":\n121\t            continue\n122\t        if _is_test_pollution_event(ev):\n123\t            test_pollution_skipped += 1\n124\t            continue\n125\t        # T-2 deferred (t5 P2): ghost/probe exemptions RETIRED — the shape\n126\t        # detectors above stay tested for a future provenance-bearing\n127\t        # emitter, but no row is skipped on caller-controlled absence.\n128\t\n129\t        # Skill-less by design: general-purpose archetype dispatches\n130\t        # (mitigated rail per ADR-082) AND built-in subagent types like\n131\t        # Explore/Plan/claude-code-guide that have no .claude/agents/<name>.md\n132\t        # and so cannot carry a `Loads <skill> skill via reference` phrase\n133\t        # (drift-detector contract per S143 lesson). Adding them to\n134\t        # _ARCHETYPE_TO_SKILL would violate the contract — exclude here instead.\n135\t        # S200: claude/claude-code-guide/statusline-setup are first-party\n136\t        # Claude Code built-ins (no .claude/agents anchor); counting them as a\n137\t        # governance gap is a false positive — exactly the FP class this filter\n138\t        # exists to prevent (else healthy claude-code-guide use trains the\n139\t        # operator to ignore the channel).\n140\t        _SKILL_LESS_BUILTINS = {\n141\t            \"general-purpose\", \"Explore\", \"Plan\",\n142\t            \"claude\", \"claude-code-guide\", \"statusline-setup\",\n143\t        }\n144\t        if (\n145\t            ev.get(\"subagent_type\") in _SKILL_LESS_BUILTINS\n146\t            and ev.get(\"archetype\") in _SKILL_LESS_BUILTINS\n147\t        ):\n148\t            skill_less_by_design += 1\n149\t            continue\n150\t        total += 1\n151\t        if ev.get(\"skill\") in (None, \"unknown\", \"\"):\n152\t            unknown += 1\n153\t    if total == 0:\n154\t        msg = (\n155\t            \"no custom-archetype spawns \"\n156\t            \"({s} general-purpose, {t} test-pollution)\".format(\n157\t                s=skill_less_by_design, t=test_pollution_skipped,\n158\t            )\n159\t        )\n160\t        return \"green\", msg, {\n161\t            \"unknown\": 0, \"total\": 0,\n162\t            \"skill_less_by_design\": skill_less_by_design,\n163\t            \"test_pollution_skipped\": test_pollution_skipped,\n164\t        }\n165\t    ratio = unknown / total\n166\t    status = \"red\" if ratio > 0.10 else \"yellow\" if ratio > 0 else \"green\"\n167\t    return status, f\"{unknown}/{total} = {ratio:.0%}\", {\n168\t        \"unknown\": unknown, \"total\": total,\n169\t        \"skill_less_by_design\": skill_less_by_design,\n170\t        \"test_pollution_skipped\": test_pollution_skipped,\n171\t    }\n172\t\n173\t\n174\tdef check_hook_live_smoke() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n175\t    \"\"\"PLAN-082 Codex Item D replacement for hook_test_baseline.\n176\t\n177\t    Drops the broken `.claude/cache/hook-tests.json` baseline (never\n178\t    populated; required pytest 12 s — not boot-budget feasible). Per\n179\t    Codex 6th-option: replace with a cheap live hook smoke — parse\n180\t    settings.json + verify referenced hook files exist + executable +\n181\t    `py_compile` cleanly. Stdlib only, no pytest.\n182\t\n183\t    Test provenance (last full pytest pass) moves to Tier-A\n184\t    (`tier_a_hook_test_baseline_age` — separate check).\n185\t    \"\"\"\n186\t    import py_compile\n187\t\n188\t    settings = REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"settings.json\"\n189\t    if not settings.exists():\n190\t        return \"yellow\", \"settings.json missing\", None\n191\t    try:\n192\t        data = json.loads(settings.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n193\t    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n194\t        return \"red\", f\"settings.json parse: {exc.__class__.__name__}\", None\n195\t\n196\t    hooks_table = data.get(\"hooks\") if isinstance(data, dict) else None\n197\t    if not isinstance(hooks_table, dict):\n198\t        return \"yellow\", \"no hooks table\", None\n199\t\n200\t    shim_re = re.compile(r\"_python-hook\\.sh[\\\"']?\\s+[\\\"']?([A-Za-z0-9_./-]+\\.py)\")\n201\t    direct_re = re.compile(r\"\\.claude/hooks/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+\\.py\")\n202\t    seen: List[str] = []\n203\t    seen_set: set = set()\n204\t    for hook_list in hooks_table.values():\n205\t        if not isinstance(hook_list, list):\n206\t            continue\n207\t        for entry in hook_list:\n208\t            if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n209\t                continue\n210\t            inner = entry.get(\"hooks\") if isinstance(entry.get(\"hooks\"), list) else []\n211\t            for cmd_obj in inner:\n212\t                if not isinstance(cmd_obj, dict):\n213\t                    continue\n214\t                cmd_str = cmd_obj.get(\"command\", \"\")\n215\t                if not isinstance(cmd_str, str):\n216\t                    continue\n217\t                refs: List[str] = []\n218\t                refs.extend(direct_re.findall(cmd_str))\n219\t                refs.extend(shim_re.findall(cmd_str))\n220\t                for raw in refs:\n221\t                    s = re.sub(r\"^\\$\\{?CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\\}?/\", \"\", raw)\n222\t                    if \"/\" not in s:\n223\t                        s = f\".claude/hooks/{s}\"\n224\t                    if s not in seen_set:\n225\t                        seen_set.add(s)\n226\t                        seen.append(s)\n227\t\n228\t    failures: List[str] = []\n229\t    checked = 0\n230\t    for rel in seen:\n231\t        path = REPO_ROOT / rel\n232\t        if not path.is_file():\n233\t            failures.append(f\"missing:{rel}\")\n234\t            continue\n235\t        try:\n236\t            py_compile.compile(str(path), doraise=True)\n237\t        except (py_compile.PyCompileError, OSError):\n238\t            failures.append(f\"compile_fail:{rel}\")\n239\t            continue\n240\t        checked += 1\n241\t\n242\t    if failures:\n243\t        return \"red\", f\"{len(failures)}/{len(seen)} hook(s) broken\", {\n244\t            \"failures\": failures[:10],  # bound for sanitization\n245\t            \"checked\": checked,\n246\t            \"total\": len(seen),\n247\t        }\n248\t    if checked == 0:\n249\t        return \"yellow\", \"no hooks discovered\", {\"checked\": 0, \"total\": 0}\n250\t    return \"green\", f\"{checked} hook(s) smoke-pass\", {\"checked\": checked, \"total\": len(seen)}\n251\t\n252\t\n253\t# Backward-compat alias — some external callers / tests may still import the\n254\t# old name. Live smoke is a strict improvement (no cache dependency, faster).\n255\tcheck_hook_test_baseline = check_hook_live_smoke\n256\t\n257\t\n258\tdef check_audit_v3_backlog() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n259\t    # PoC: count plans with audit_v3_* tags still open\n260\t    plans = _get_plan_paths()\n261\t    backlog: List[str] = []\n262\t    for p in plans:\n263\t        try:\n264\t            text = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n265\t        except OSError:\n266\t            continue\n267\t        m = re.match(r\"^---\\s*\\n(.*?)\\n---\\s*\\n\", text, re.DOTALL)\n268\t        if not m:\n269\t            continue\n270\t        front = m.group(1)\n271\t        if \"audit_v3\" in front and not re.search(r\"^status:\\s*done\\s*$\", front, re.MULTILINE):\n272\t            backlog.append(p.stem)\n273\t    return (\"yellow\" if backlog else \"green\", f\"{len(backlog)} open\", backlog)\n274\t\n275\t\n276\t# ---- Padrões de sentinel: DERIVADOS da autoridade (S321) -------------------\n277\t# Este check varria UM único padrão (`PLAN-*/architect/round-*/approved.md`)\n278\t# enquanto `check_canonical_edit.py` reconhece DEZ. Consequência medida: uma\n279\t# cerimônia preparada como `PLAN-182/wave-w1-followup-approved.md` — formato\n280\t# válido e aceito pelo guard — nunca aparecia no digest de boot, e o check\n281\t# reportava \"0 pending\" com um sentinel esperando assinatura. Guard verde que\n282\t# não vê o alvo.\n283\t#\n284\t# A cura NÃO é copiar a lista para cá: uma segunda cópia envelhece em\n285\t# silêncio, que é a classe que este repo caça. Os padrões são EXTRAÍDOS por\n286\t# AST do arquivo que os define. `_PATTERNS` é local a uma função lá, então\n287\t# não dá para importar — o AST é o mecanismo, não a aparência.\n288\t#\n289\t# Fail-open com VOZ: se a extração falhar, cai num conjunto mínimo E o\n290\t# summary declara que está em fallback. Um degradê silencioso reproduziria o\n291\t# defeito que esta função existe para curar.\n292\t_SENTINEL_PATTERNS_FALLBACK = (\n293\t    \"PLAN-*/architect/round-*/approved.md\",\n294\t    \"PLAN-*/approved.md\",\n295\t    \"PLAN-*/wave-*-approved.md\",\n296\t    \"PLAN-*/approved-amendment-*.md\",\n297\t)\n298\t\n299\t\n300\tdef _sentinel_patterns() -> Tuple[Tuple[str, ...], bool]:\n301\t    \"\"\"(padrões, derived) — `derived=False` sinaliza fallback.\"\"\"\n302\t    import ast\n303\t\n304\t    src_path = REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"hooks\" / \"check_canonical_edit.py\"\n305\t    try:\n306\t        tree = ast.parse(src_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n307\t    except Exception:\n308\t        return _SENTINEL_PATTERNS_FALLBACK, False\n309\t    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n310\t        if not isinstance(node, ast.Assign):\n311\t            continue\n312\t        names = [t.id for t in node.targets if isinstance(t, ast.Name)]\n313\t        if \"_PATTERNS\" not in names:\n314\t            continue\n315\t        try:\n316\t            value = ast.literal_eval(node.value)\n317\t        except Exception:\n318\t            continue\n319\t        pats = tuple(\n320\t            p for p in value\n321\t            if isinstance(p, str) and p.startswith(\"PLAN-\")\n322\t        )\n323\t        if pats:\n324\t            return pats, True\n325\t    return _SENTINEL_PATTERNS_FALLBACK, False\n326\t\n327\t\n328\tdef check_sentinels_pending_gpg() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n329\t    \"\"\"Count GPG-pending sentinels post-cutoff.\n330\t\n331\t    Codex S82 P2 fix: previous impl scanned ALL historical sentinels with no\n332\t    date cutoff → 30+ pending entries every boot from PLAN-030/031/039 round-1\n333\t    pre-enforcement era. Now applies SENTINEL_CUTOFF_EPOCH (2026-04-22) to\n334\t    skip legacy. Also Codex S82 P2 sorted glob for CR-N7 stable ordering.\n335\t    \"\"\"\n336\t    pending: List[str] = []\n337\t    plans_dir = REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"plans\"\n338\t    patterns, derived = _sentinel_patterns()\n339\t    for pat in patterns:\n340\t        for approved in sorted(plans_dir.glob(pat)):\n341\t            try:\n342\t                mtime = approved.stat().st_mtime\n343\t            except OSError:\n344\t                continue\n345\t            if mtime < SENTINEL_CUTOFF_EPOCH:\n346\t                continue  # pre-enforcement legacy\n347\t            # S321: o `.asc` acompanha o ARQUIVO, não um `approved.md` fixo\n348\t            # no diretório. A forma antiga (`parent / \"approved.md.asc\"`)\n349\t            # só funcionava para o padrão `.../approved.md` e teria dado\n350\t            # falso-pendente para `wave-*-approved.md`.\n351\t            if not approved.with_name(approved.name + \".asc\").exists():\n352\t                rel = str(approved.relative_to(REPO_ROOT))\n353\t                if rel not in pending:\n354\t                    pending.append(rel)\n355\t    pending.sort()  # CR-N7 ordenação estável\n356\t    note = \"\" if derived else \" [padrões em FALLBACK — a autoridade não foi lida]\"\n357\t    return (\n358\t        \"yellow\" if pending else \"green\",\n359\t        f\"{len(pending)} pending{note}\",\n360\t        pending,\n361\t    )\n362\t\n363\t\n364\tdef check_rc_hold_aged() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n365\t    release_md = REPO_ROOT / \"RELEASE.md\"\n366\t    rc_hold = REPO_ROOT / \"RC-HOLD.md\"\n367\t    target = release_md if release_md.exists() else rc_hold if rc_hold.exists() else None\n368\t    if target is None:\n369\t        return \"green\", \"no rc-hold doc\", None\n370\t    text = target.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n371\t    # PoC: count rc-hold-waiver entries (real impl would parse dates)\n372\t    n = len(re.findall(r\"rc-hold-waiver\", text))\n373\t    return (\"yellow\" if n else \"green\", f\"{n} rc-hold-waiver entries\", n)\n374\t\n375\t\n376\t# E7-F5 (PLAN-120-FOLLOWUP): real daily-USD burn-rate thresholds.\n377\t# Previously this check returned \"green\" unconditionally (Potemkin stub) — it\n378\t# tallied cost_usd over 24h but never compared it against a budget, so a\n379\t# runaway burn never surfaced at boot. We now apply a yellow/red ceiling.\n380\t# Both bounds are env-overridable (adopter sessions differ wildly in cost);\n381\t# defaults are calibrated to a typical heavy CEO session. Fail-OPEN: any\n382\t# parse/lookup error degrades to the default ceiling, never raises, and an\n383\t# empty/zero-cost log stays green (the steady-state).\n384\t_COST_YELLOW_USD_DEFAULT = 50.0\n385\t_COST_RED_USD_DEFAULT = 150.0\n386\t\n387\t\n388\tdef _cost_threshold(env_var: str, default: float) -> float:\n389\t    \"\"\"Read a positive float ceiling from env; fall back to default fail-open.\"\"\"\n390\t    raw = os.environ.get(env_var, \"\")\n391\t    if not raw:\n392\t        return default\n393\t    try:\n394\t        val = float(raw.strip())\n395\t    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n396\t        return default\n397\t    # Reject non-finite / non-positive overrides (would defeat the gate).\n398\t    if val != val or val == float(\"inf\") or val <= 0:\n399\t        return default\n400\t    return val\n401\t\n402\t\n403\tdef check_cost_24h_usd() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n404\t    \"\"\"Sum cost_usd over 24h and gate against env-overridable USD ceilings.\n405\t\n406\t    yellow at CEO_BOOT_COST_YELLOW_USD (default $50/24h); red at\n407\t    CEO_BOOT_COST_RED_USD (default $150/24h). Fail-open: no cost datapoints\n408\t    or unreadable log => green. Thresholds are advisory burn-rate alerts\n409\t    (ADR-064 50/80/95% doctrine), never a hard block.\n410\t    \"\"\"\n411\t    total = 0.0\n412\t    samples = 0\n413\t    for ev in _iter_audit_events_since(24):\n414\t        c = ev.get(\"cost_usd\")\n415\t        if isinstance(c, (int, float)) and not isinstance(c, bool):\n416\t            total += float(c)\n417\t            samples += 1\n418\t    yellow = _cost_threshold(\"CEO_BOOT_COST_YELLOW_USD\", _COST_YELLOW_USD_DEFAULT)\n419\t    red = _cost_threshold(\"CEO_BOOT_COST_RED_USD\", _COST_RED_USD_DEFAULT)\n420\t    # Guard against an inverted override (yellow >= red): keep red as the\n421\t    # higher bound so the status ladder stays monotonic.\n422\t    if yellow >= red:\n423\t        yellow = min(yellow, red)\n424\t    if samples == 0:\n425\t        status = \"green\"\n426\t    elif total >= red:\n427\t        status = \"red\"\n428\t    elif total >= yellow:\n429\t        status = \"yellow\"\n430\t    else:\n431\t        status = \"green\"\n432\t    return status, f\"${total:.2f}/24h\", {\n433\t        \"total_usd\": round(total, 4),\n434\t        \"samples\": samples,\n435\t        \"yellow_usd\": yellow,\n436\t        \"red_usd\": red,\n437\t    }\n438\t\n439\t\n440\tdef check_active_plan_burn_ratio() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n441\t    # PoC: find first executing plan, parse budget_tokens, sum tokens from log\n442\t    _, _, executing = check_plans_executing()\n443\t    if not executing:\n444\t        return \"green\", \"no active plan\", None\n445\t    plan_id = executing[0].split(\"-\")[0] + \"-\" + executing[0].split(\"-\")[1] if executing else None\n446\t    if not plan_id:\n447\t        return \"green\", \"no plan id\", None\n448\t    plan_path = REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"plans\" / f\"{executing[0]}.md\"\n449\t    try:\n450\t        text = plan_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n451\t    except OSError:\n452\t        return \"yellow\", \"plan unreadable\", None\n453\t    m = re.search(r\"^budget_tokens:\\s*(.+?)$\", text, re.MULTILINE)\n454\t    if not m:\n455\t        return \"yellow\", \"no budget_tokens\", None\n456\t    return \"green\", f\"budget {m.group(1).strip()}\", {\"plan\": plan_id, \"budget_raw\": m.group(1).strip()}\n457\t\n458\t\n459\tdef check_adrs_stale_proposed() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n460\t    adrs = sorted((REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"adr\").glob(\"ADR-*.md\"))\n461\t    proposed_old: List[str] = []\n462\t    now = time.time()\n463\t    for a in adrs:\n464\t        try:\n465\t            text = a.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n466\t            mtime = a.stat().st_mtime\n467\t        except OSError:\n468\t            continue\n469\t        m = re.match(r\"^---\\s*\\n(.*?)\\n---\\s*\\n\", text, re.DOTALL)\n470\t        if not m:\n471\t            continue\n472\t        if re.search(r\"^status:\\s*proposed\\s*$\", m.group(1), re.MULTILINE):\n473\t            age_d = (now - mtime) / 86400\n474\t            if age_d > 30:\n475\t                proposed_old.append(a.stem)\n476\t    return (\"yellow\" if proposed_old else \"green\", f\"{len(proposed_old)} proposed >30d\", proposed_old)\n477\t\n478\t\n479\t# ---- 11 Tier-A checks (--verbose mode; PLAN-065 §4.3.3) ------------------\n480\t# Selection rationale (each picked for high signal-to-cost ratio + non-overlap\n481\t# with Tier-S; see PLAN-065 §4.3.3):\n482\t#   tier_a_debate_transcripts     — debate hygiene (Round-1 archetype output)\n483\t#   tier_a_lessons_30d            — lesson velocity (memory growth pulse)\n484\t#   tier_a_spec_version_drift     — VERSION ↔ SPEC/v*/VERSION mismatch\n485\t#   tier_a_npm_version_match      — package.json vs VERSION mismatch\n486\t#   tier_a_waivers_count          — waivers/*.md aggregate (rc-hold + cosmetic)\n487\t#   tier_a_adrs_recent_status     — ADR-098..104 reservation slots tracking\n488\t#   tier_a_cache_hit_rate_24h     — ceo-boot-emitted cache_hit ratio (self-loop)\n489\t#   tier_a_hook_test_baseline_age — last-cached hook-test baseline age (S81 cache)\n490\t#   tier_a_sentinel_signers_tracked — .claude/state/sentinel-signers.txt git-tracked?\n491\t#   tier_a_gitignore_state_excluded — .gitignore covers state/ dir?\n492\t#   tier_a_model_currency         — PLAN-176 W3a trio per lane (advisory, offline)\n493\t\n494\t\n495\tdef check_tier_a_debate_transcripts() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n496\t    \"\"\"Count debate transcripts produced in last 24h (forensic hygiene).\"\"\"\n497\t    debate_root = REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"plans\"\n498\t    n = 0\n499\t    cutoff = time.time() - 86400\n500\t    for transcript in debate_root.rglob(\"debate/*/round-*.md\"):\n501\t        try:\n502\t            if transcript.stat().st_mtime >= cutoff:\n503\t                n += 1\n504\t        except OSError:\n505\t            continue\n506\t    # Status green regardless — informational. Yellow if zero AND there is an\n507\t    # executing plan (suggests work without debate trail).\n508\t    _, _, executing = check_plans_executing()\n509\t    if n == 0 and executing:\n510\t        return \"yellow\", f\"0 transcripts/24h ({len(executing)} executing)\", n\n511\t    return \"green\", f\"{n} transcripts/24h\", n\n512\t\n513\t\n514\t# CEO-INFORMATIONAL-ONLY: velocidade de licoes, docstring ja diz informational\n515\tdef check_tier_a_lessons_30d() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n516\t    \"\"\"Count lessons added in memory dir over 30d (informational).\"\"\"\n517\t    # Derive the Claude Code project slug from the project dir (absolute path\n518\t    # with \"/\" -> \"-\") instead of hard-coding the meta-repo's slug, so this\n519\t    # resolves correctly in any install. (Previously hard-coded the Owner's\n520\t    # absolute home path, which broke for every other install and tripped the\n521\t    # contamination guard.)\n522\t    project_dir = os.environ.get(\"CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\") or os.getcwd()\n523\t    slug = _rp.project_slug(project_dir)  # PLAN-182 W3 (S321): slug via resolvedor unico, nunca re-derivado\n524\t    mem_dir = Path.home() / \".claude\" / \"projects\" / slug / \"memory\"\n525\t    if not mem_dir.exists():\n526\t        return \"green\", \"memory dir absent\", 0\n527\t    cutoff = time.time() - 30 * 86400\n528\t    n = 0\n529\t    for f in mem_dir.glob(\"*.md\"):\n530\t        try:\n531\t            if f.stat().st_mtime >= cutoff:\n532\t                n += 1\n533\t        except OSError:\n534\t            continue\n535\t    return \"green\", f\"{n} lessons/30d\", n\n536\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95a0ebeb-18f5-4176-8f95-2931dd13a332","uuid":"728739ad-2b7b-4d77-8412-bc5da8f9f1a2","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:46:12.243Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py","content":"\"\"\"Extracted ceo-boot declarations executed by the facade.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\n\n\n# PLAN-177 t2 (re-pass rc.4 P1-f). The POSITIVE half of the probe test.\n#\n# The S303 filter below identified a probe by ABSENCE alone — five governed\n# markers missing — and absence is the shape of the events the ratio exists to\n# find: a markerless real spawn (including one the PreToolUse hook admitted by\n# failing open) was classified as harness noise and removed from the\n# denominator. A probe-only window then reported green with\n# `harness_probes_skipped=1` while the governance gap it was built to surface\n# went unrendered.\n#\n# So the structural conditions are necessary, not sufficient: the row must ALSO\n# carry the observed harness signature. The signature is CLOSED — the literal\n# description the tool-materialization probe emits, anchored at both ends\n# (`Load <Tool> via ToolSearch?`, S303 observation, prompt `noop`) — plus\n# corroboration by `desc_hash`, which the emitter computes over the RAW\n# description: if the two disagree the preview was truncated or redacted, i.e.\n# not this short, secret-free probe line. Anything else counts. Every\n# uncertainty resolves toward VISIBLE.\n_HARNESS_PROBE_DESC_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\ALoad [A-Za-z0-9_.\\-]+(?:,[ ]?[A-Za-z0-9_.\\-]+)* via ToolSearch\\?\\Z\"\n)\n\n\ndef _has_harness_probe_fingerprint(ev: Dict[str, Any]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"True iff the row carries the CLOSED, observed harness-probe signature.\n\n    Positive identification, never inferred from missing fields. An absent or\n    non-matching `desc_hash` is NOT corroboration, so it returns False and the\n    row is counted — the safe direction for an advisory that exists to expose\n    unclassified spawns.\n    \"\"\"\n    desc = ev.get(\"desc_preview\")\n    if not isinstance(desc, str) or not _HARNESS_PROBE_DESC_RE.match(desc):\n        return False\n    digest = ev.get(\"desc_hash\")\n    if not isinstance(digest, str) or not digest:\n        return False\n    return digest == hashlib.sha256(desc.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef _is_harness_probe_event(ev: Dict[str, Any]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"True iff the agent_spawn row is a harness-internal tool-loading probe.\n\n    S303: the ghost filter above was written for the ToolSearch probes of an\n    older harness, whose Agent-shaped PostToolUse rows carried NO description\n    (desc_preview == \"\" and desc_hash == SHA256(b\"\")). The current harness\n    supplies a human-readable description for the same class of call — e.g.\n    ``Load WebFetch via ToolSearch?`` with prompt ``noop`` and a fixed cheap\n    model — so all four ghost conditions no longer hold and a pure\n    tool-materialization probe lands in the denominator as a governance gap.\n\n    The discriminator is ``subagent_type``: the Agent/Task spawn contract makes\n    it REQUIRED for every governed dispatch (``check_agent_spawn.py`` derives\n    the authoritative archetype from it, and ``extract_skill`` Path D needs it),\n    so a row that carries none was never a CEO dispatch. All five conditions\n    must hold — no subagent_type, no archetype, no rail attribution, no\n    ``## AGENT PROFILE`` and no ``## FILE ASSIGNMENT`` — so a real named spawn\n    that merely lost one field still counts.\n\n    T-2 STATUS (re-pass rc.4 t5/t7 P2): DEFERRED, not cured — this function\n    ALWAYS returns False today and probe-shaped rows COUNT in the\n    denominator (a probe-only window reads 1/1 red and the operator\n    triages it). The former ``harness_probes_skipped`` counter was removed\n    together with the exemption; no row is skipped, so nothing is\n    \"reported through\" anything.\n\n    PLAN-177 t2 (P1-f): those five are NECESSARY, NOT SUFFICIENT. Absence is\n    exactly the shape of the event this ratio exists to expose — a markerless\n    REAL spawn, including one admitted because the PreToolUse hook failed\n    open, matched all five and was deleted from the denominator. The row must\n    ALSO carry the closed harness signature\n    (``_has_harness_probe_fingerprint``); an unrecognised description counts,\n    however markerless the row is.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Re-pass rc.4 t2 (P1): the S303 exemption is RETIRED until trusted\n    # provenance exists. `desc_preview` and `desc_hash` are both derived\n    # from the same CALLER-CONTROLLED description, so the hash corroborates\n    # nothing: a real markerless spawn described as\n    # `Load WebFetch via ToolSearch?` was silently deleted from the\n    # denominator — the exact event this ratio exists to expose. Until the\n    # EMITTER can stamp provenance the caller cannot forge, probe-shaped\n    # rows COUNT (the conservative direction for an advisory: a yellow the\n    # operator triages beats a green that hides a fail-open spawn).\n    # _has_harness_probe_fingerprint is kept (tested) as the shape\n    # DETECTOR for that future provenance-bearing emitter.\n    return False\n\n\ndef check_skill_unknown_ratio() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Detect spawns that should have SKILL injection but didn't.\n\n    S94 follow-up: excludes intentionally skill-less archetypes —\n    `general-purpose` subagent dispatches via the mitigated rail\n    (ADR-082) by design have no SKILL.md anchor. They broker cross-\n    LLM gate calls and similar utility work; counting them as FPs\n    inflates the ratio to 100% during healthy Codex MCP sessions\n    and trains the operator to ignore the channel.\n\n    A spawn counts as \"skill missing\" ONLY when its `archetype` is\n    a custom (non-general-purpose) one AND `skill` is unknown/empty.\n    That is the original PLAN-020 ADR-051 governance gap the\n    detector was built for.\n    \"\"\"\n    # T-2 STATUS (re-pass rc.4 t5 P2): DEFERRED, not cured. Both the S86\n    # ghost filter and the S303 probe filter are RETIRED (absence-based,\n    # caller-forgeable); every agent_spawn row counts until the EMITTER can\n    # stamp provenance the caller cannot forge. The skipped counters were\n    # removed with them — a permanently-zero counter reads as \"filter\n    # active, nothing skipped\", which is the wrong claim.\n    total = 0\n    unknown = 0\n    skill_less_by_design = 0\n    test_pollution_skipped = 0\n    for ev in _iter_audit_events_since(24):\n        if ev.get(\"action\") != \"agent_spawn\":\n            continue\n        if _is_test_pollution_event(ev):\n            test_pollution_skipped += 1\n            continue\n        # T-2 deferred (t5 P2): ghost/probe exemptions RETIRED — the shape\n        # detectors above stay tested for a future provenance-bearing\n        # emitter, but no row is skipped on caller-controlled absence.\n\n        # Skill-less by design: general-purpose archetype dispatches\n        # (mitigated rail per ADR-082) AND built-in subagent types like\n        # Explore/Plan/claude-code-guide that have no .claude/agents/<name>.md\n        # and so cannot carry a `Loads <skill> skill via reference` phrase\n        # (drift-detector contract per S143 lesson). Adding them to\n        # _ARCHETYPE_TO_SKILL would violate the contract — exclude here instead.\n        # S200: claude/claude-code-guide/statusline-setup are first-party\n        # Claude Code built-ins (no .claude/agents anchor); counting them as a\n        # governance gap is a false positive — exactly the FP class this filter\n        # exists to prevent (else healthy claude-code-guide use trains the\n        # operator to ignore the channel).\n        _SKILL_LESS_BUILTINS = {\n            \"general-purpose\", \"Explore\", \"Plan\",\n            \"claude\", \"claude-code-guide\", \"statusline-setup\",\n        }\n        if (\n            ev.get(\"subagent_type\") in _SKILL_LESS_BUILTINS\n            and ev.get(\"archetype\") in _SKILL_LESS_BUILTINS\n        ):\n            skill_less_by_design += 1\n            continue\n        total += 1\n        if ev.get(\"skill\") in (None, \"unknown\", \"\"):\n            unknown += 1\n    if total == 0:\n        msg = (\n            \"no custom-archetype spawns \"\n            \"({s} general-purpose, {t} test-pollution)\".format(\n                s=skill_less_by_design, t=test_pollution_skipped,\n            )\n        )\n        return \"green\", msg, {\n            \"unknown\": 0, \"total\": 0,\n            \"skill_less_by_design\": skill_less_by_design,\n            \"test_pollution_skipped\": test_pollution_skipped,\n        }\n    ratio = unknown / total\n    status = \"red\" if ratio > 0.10 else \"yellow\" if ratio > 0 else \"green\"\n    return status, f\"{unknown}/{total} = {ratio:.0%}\", {\n        \"unknown\": unknown, \"total\": total,\n        \"skill_less_by_design\": skill_less_by_design,\n        \"test_pollution_skipped\": test_pollution_skipped,\n    }\n\n\ndef check_hook_live_smoke() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"PLAN-082 Codex Item D replacement for hook_test_baseline.\n\n    Drops the broken `.claude/cache/hook-tests.json` baseline (never\n    populated; required pytest 12 s — not boot-budget feasible). Per\n    Codex 6th-option: replace with a cheap live hook smoke — parse\n    settings.json + verify referenced hook files exist + executable +\n    `py_compile` cleanly. Stdlib only, no pytest.\n\n    Test provenance (last full pytest pass) moves to Tier-A\n    (`tier_a_hook_test_baseline_age` — separate check).\n    \"\"\"\n    import py_compile\n\n    settings = REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"settings.json\"\n    if not settings.exists():\n        return \"yellow\", \"settings.json missing\", None\n    try:\n        data = json.loads(settings.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n        return \"red\", f\"settings.json parse: {exc.__class__.__name__}\", None\n\n    hooks_table = data.get(\"hooks\") if isinstance(data, dict) else None\n    if not isinstance(hooks_table, dict):\n        return \"yellow\", \"no hooks table\", None\n\n    shim_re = re.compile(r\"_python-hook\\.sh[\\\"']?\\s+[\\\"']?([A-Za-z0-9_./-]+\\.py)\")\n    direct_re = re.compile(r\"\\.claude/hooks/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+\\.py\")\n    seen: List[str] = []\n    seen_set: set = set()\n    for hook_list in hooks_table.values():\n        if not isinstance(hook_list, list):\n            continue\n        for entry in hook_list:\n            if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n                continue\n            inner = entry.get(\"hooks\") if isinstance(entry.get(\"hooks\"), list) else []\n            for cmd_obj in inner:\n                if not isinstance(cmd_obj, dict):\n                    continue\n                cmd_str = cmd_obj.get(\"command\", \"\")\n                if not isinstance(cmd_str, str):\n                    continue\n                refs: List[str] = []\n                refs.extend(direct_re.findall(cmd_str))\n                refs.extend(shim_re.findall(cmd_str))\n                for raw in refs:\n                    s = re.sub(r\"^\\$\\{?CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\\}?/\", \"\", raw)\n                    if \"/\" not in s:\n                        s = f\".claude/hooks/{s}\"\n                    if s not in seen_set:\n                        seen_set.add(s)\n                        seen.append(s)\n\n    failures: List[str] = []\n    checked = 0\n    for rel in seen:\n        path = REPO_ROOT / rel\n        if not path.is_file():\n            failures.append(f\"missing:{rel}\")\n            continue\n        try:\n            py_compile.compile(str(path), doraise=True)\n        except (py_compile.PyCompileError, OSError):\n            failures.append(f\"compile_fail:{rel}\")\n            continue\n        checked += 1\n\n    if failures:\n        return \"red\", f\"{len(failures)}/{len(seen)} hook(s) broken\", {\n            \"failures\": failures[:10],  # bound for sanitization\n            \"checked\": checked,\n            \"total\": len(seen),\n        }\n    if checked == 0:\n        return \"yellow\", \"no hooks discovered\", {\"checked\": 0, \"total\": 0}\n    return \"green\", f\"{checked} hook(s) smoke-pass\", {\"checked\": checked, \"total\": len(seen)}\n\n\n# Backward-compat alias — some external callers / tests may still import the\n# old name. Live smoke is a strict improvement (no cache dependency, faster).\ncheck_hook_test_baseline = check_hook_live_smoke\n\n\ndef check_audit_v3_backlog() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n    # PoC: count plans with audit_v3_* tags still open\n    plans = _get_plan_paths()\n    backlog: List[str] = []\n    for p in plans:\n        try:\n            text = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        except OSError:\n            continue\n        m = re.match(r\"^---\\s*\\n(.*?)\\n---\\s*\\n\", text, re.DOTALL)\n        if not m:\n            continue\n        front = m.group(1)\n        if \"audit_v3\" in front and not re.search(r\"^status:\\s*done\\s*$\", front, re.MULTILINE):\n            backlog.append(p.stem)\n    return (\"yellow\" if backlog else \"green\", f\"{len(backlog)} open\", backlog)\n\n\n# ---- Padrões de sentinel: DERIVADOS da autoridade (S321) -------------------\n# Este check varria UM único padrão (`PLAN-*/architect/round-*/approved.md`)\n# enquanto `check_canonical_edit.py` reconhece DEZ. Consequência medida: uma\n# cerimônia preparada como `PLAN-182/wave-w1-followup-approved.md` — formato\n# válido e aceito pelo guard — nunca aparecia no digest de boot, e o check\n# reportava \"0 pending\" com um sentinel esperando assinatura. Guard verde que\n# não vê o alvo.\n#\n# A cura NÃO é copiar a lista para cá: uma segunda cópia envelhece em\n# silêncio, que é a classe que este repo caça. Os padrões são EXTRAÍDOS por\n# AST do arquivo que os define. `_PATTERNS` é local a uma função lá, então\n# não dá para importar — o AST é o mecanismo, não a aparência.\n#\n# Fail-open com VOZ: se a extração falhar, cai num conjunto mínimo E o\n# summary declara que está em fallback. Um degradê silencioso reproduziria o\n# defeito que esta função existe para curar.\n_SENTINEL_PATTERNS_FALLBACK = (\n    \"PLAN-*/architect/round-*/approved.md\",\n    \"PLAN-*/approved.md\",\n    \"PLAN-*/wave-*-approved.md\",\n    \"PLAN-*/approved-amendment-*.md\",\n)\n\n\ndef _sentinel_patterns() -> Tuple[Tuple[str, ...], bool]:\n    \"\"\"(padrões, derived) — `derived=False` sinaliza fallback.\"\"\"\n    import ast\n\n    src_path = REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"hooks\" / \"check_canonical_edit.py\"\n    try:\n        tree = ast.parse(src_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except Exception:\n        return _SENTINEL_PATTERNS_FALLBACK, False\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        if not isinstance(node, ast.Assign):\n            continue\n        names = [t.id for t in node.targets if isinstance(t, ast.Name)]\n        if \"_PATTERNS\" not in names:\n            continue\n        try:\n            value = ast.literal_eval(node.value)\n        except Exception:\n            continue\n        pats = tuple(\n            p for p in value\n            if isinstance(p, str) and p.startswith(\"PLAN-\")\n        )\n        if pats:\n            return pats, True\n    return _SENTINEL_PATTERNS_FALLBACK, False\n\n\ndef check_sentinels_pending_gpg() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Count GPG-pending sentinels post-cutoff.\n\n    Codex S82 P2 fix: previous impl scanned ALL historical sentinels with no\n    date cutoff → 30+ pending entries every boot from PLAN-030/031/039 round-1\n    pre-enforcement era. Now applies SENTINEL_CUTOFF_EPOCH (2026-04-22) to\n    skip legacy. Also Codex S82 P2 sorted glob for CR-N7 stable ordering.\n    \"\"\"\n    pending: List[str] = []\n    plans_dir = REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"plans\"\n    patterns, derived = _sentinel_patterns()\n    for pat in patterns:\n        for approved in sorted(plans_dir.glob(pat)):\n            try:\n                mtime = approved.stat().st_mtime\n            except OSError:\n                continue\n            if mtime < SENTINEL_CUTOFF_EPOCH:\n                continue  # pre-enforcement legacy\n            # S321: o `.asc` acompanha o ARQUIVO, não um `approved.md` fixo\n            # no diretório. A forma antiga (`parent / \"approved.md.asc\"`)\n            # só funcionava para o padrão `.../approved.md` e teria dado\n            # falso-pendente para `wave-*-approved.md`.\n            if not approved.with_name(approved.name + \".asc\").exists():\n                rel = str(approved.relative_to(REPO_ROOT))\n                if rel not in pending:\n                    pending.append(rel)\n    pending.sort()  # CR-N7 ordenação estável\n    note = \"\" if derived else \" [padrões em FALLBACK — a autoridade não foi lida]\"\n    return (\n        \"yellow\" if pending else \"green\",\n        f\"{len(pending)} pending{note}\",\n        pending,\n    )\n\n\ndef check_rc_hold_aged() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n    release_md = REPO_ROOT / \"RELEASE.md\"\n    rc_hold = REPO_ROOT / \"RC-HOLD.md\"\n    target = release_md if release_md.exists() else rc_hold if rc_hold.exists() else None\n    if target is None:\n        return \"green\", \"no rc-hold doc\", None\n    text = target.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    # PoC: count rc-hold-waiver entries (real impl would parse dates)\n    n = len(re.findall(r\"rc-hold-waiver\", text))\n    return (\"yellow\" if n else \"green\", f\"{n} rc-hold-waiver entries\", n)\n\n\n# E7-F5 (PLAN-120-FOLLOWUP): real daily-USD burn-rate thresholds.\n# Previously this check returned \"green\" unconditionally (Potemkin stub) — it\n# tallied cost_usd over 24h but never compared it against a budget, so a\n# runaway burn never surfaced at boot. We now apply a yellow/red ceiling.\n# Both bounds are env-overridable (adopter sessions differ wildly in cost);\n# defaults are calibrated to a typical heavy CEO session. Fail-OPEN: any\n# parse/lookup error degrades to the default ceiling, never raises, and an\n# empty/zero-cost log stays green (the steady-state).\n_COST_YELLOW_USD_DEFAULT = 50.0\n_COST_RED_USD_DEFAULT = 150.0\n\n\ndef _cost_threshold(env_var: str, default: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Read a positive float ceiling from env; fall back to default fail-open.\"\"\"\n    raw = os.environ.get(env_var, \"\")\n    if not raw:\n        return default\n    try:\n        val = float(raw.strip())\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        return default\n    # Reject non-finite / non-positive overrides (would defeat the gate).\n    if val != val or val == float(\"inf\") or val <= 0:\n        return default\n    return val\n\n\ndef check_cost_24h_usd() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Sum cost_usd over 24h and gate against env-overridable USD ceilings.\n\n    yellow at CEO_BOOT_COST_YELLOW_USD (default $50/24h); red at\n    CEO_BOOT_COST_RED_USD (default $150/24h). Fail-open: no cost datapoints\n    or unreadable log => green. Thresholds are advisory burn-rate alerts\n    (ADR-064 50/80/95% doctrine), never a hard block.\n    \"\"\"\n    total = 0.0\n    samples = 0\n    for ev in _iter_audit_events_since(24):\n        c = ev.get(\"cost_usd\")\n        if isinstance(c, (int, float)) and not isinstance(c, bool):\n            total += float(c)\n            samples += 1\n    yellow = _cost_threshold(\"CEO_BOOT_COST_YELLOW_USD\", _COST_YELLOW_USD_DEFAULT)\n    red = _cost_threshold(\"CEO_BOOT_COST_RED_USD\", _COST_RED_USD_DEFAULT)\n    # Guard against an inverted override (yellow >= red): keep red as the\n    # higher bound so the status ladder stays monotonic.\n    if yellow >= red:\n        yellow = min(yellow, red)\n    if samples == 0:\n        status = \"green\"\n    elif total >= red:\n        status = \"red\"\n    elif total >= yellow:\n        status = \"yellow\"\n    else:\n        status = \"green\"\n    return status, f\"${total:.2f}/24h\", {\n        \"total_usd\": round(total, 4),\n        \"samples\": samples,\n        \"yellow_usd\": yellow,\n        \"red_usd\": red,\n    }\n\n\ndef check_active_plan_burn_ratio() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n    # PoC: find first executing plan, parse budget_tokens, sum tokens from log\n    _, _, executing = check_plans_executing()\n    if not executing:\n        return \"green\", \"no active plan\", None\n    plan_id = executing[0].split(\"-\")[0] + \"-\" + executing[0].split(\"-\")[1] if executing else None\n    if not plan_id:\n        return \"green\", \"no plan id\", None\n    plan_path = REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"plans\" / f\"{executing[0]}.md\"\n    try:\n        text = plan_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    except OSError:\n        return \"yellow\", \"plan unreadable\", None\n    m = re.search(r\"^budget_tokens:\\s*(.+?)$\", text, re.MULTILINE)\n    if not m:\n        return \"yellow\", \"no budget_tokens\", None\n    return \"green\", f\"budget {m.group(1).strip()}\", {\"plan\": plan_id, \"budget_raw\": m.group(1).strip()}\n\n\ndef check_adrs_stale_proposed() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n    adrs = sorted((REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"adr\").glob(\"ADR-*.md\"))\n    proposed_old: List[str] = []\n    now = time.time()\n    for a in adrs:\n        try:\n            text = a.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n            mtime = a.stat().st_mtime\n        except OSError:\n            continue\n        m = re.match(r\"^---\\s*\\n(.*?)\\n---\\s*\\n\", text, re.DOTALL)\n        if not m:\n            continue\n        if re.search(r\"^status:\\s*proposed\\s*$\", m.group(1), re.MULTILINE):\n            age_d = (now - mtime) / 86400\n            if age_d > 30:\n                proposed_old.append(a.stem)\n    return (\"yellow\" if proposed_old else \"green\", f\"{len(proposed_old)} proposed >30d\", proposed_old)\n\n\n# ---- 11 Tier-A checks (--verbose mode; PLAN-065 §4.3.3) ------------------\n# Selection rationale (each picked for high signal-to-cost ratio + non-overlap\n# with Tier-S; see PLAN-065 §4.3.3):\n#   tier_a_debate_transcripts     — debate hygiene (Round-1 archetype output)\n#   tier_a_lessons_30d            — lesson velocity (memory growth pulse)\n#   tier_a_spec_version_drift     — VERSION ↔ SPEC/v*/VERSION mismatch\n#   tier_a_npm_version_match      — package.json vs VERSION mismatch\n#   tier_a_waivers_count          — waivers/*.md aggregate (rc-hold + cosmetic)\n#   tier_a_adrs_recent_status     — ADR-098..104 reservation slots tracking\n#   tier_a_cache_hit_rate_24h     — ceo-boot-emitted cache_hit ratio (self-loop)\n#   tier_a_hook_test_baseline_age — last-cached hook-test baseline age (S81 cache)\n#   tier_a_sentinel_signers_tracked — .claude/state/sentinel-signers.txt git-tracked?\n#   tier_a_gitignore_state_excluded — .gitignore covers state/ dir?\n#   tier_a_model_currency         — PLAN-176 W3a trio per lane (advisory, offline)\n\n\ndef check_tier_a_debate_transcripts() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Count debate transcripts produced in last 24h (forensic hygiene).\"\"\"\n    debate_root = REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"plans\"\n    n = 0\n    cutoff = time.time() - 86400\n    for transcript in debate_root.rglob(\"debate/*/round-*.md\"):\n        try:\n            if transcript.stat().st_mtime >= cutoff:\n                n += 1\n        except OSError:\n            continue\n    # Status green regardless — informational. Yellow if zero AND there is an\n    # executing plan (suggests work without debate trail).\n    _, _, executing = check_plans_executing()\n    if n == 0 and executing:\n        return \"yellow\", f\"0 transcripts/24h ({len(executing)} executing)\", n\n    return \"green\", f\"{n} transcripts/24h\", n\n\n\n# CEO-INFORMATIONAL-ONLY: velocidade de licoes, docstring ja diz informational\ndef check_tier_a_lessons_30d() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Count lessons added in memory dir over 30d (informational).\"\"\"\n    # Derive the Claude Code project slug from the project dir (absolute path\n    # with \"/\" -> \"-\") instead of hard-coding the meta-repo's slug, so this\n    # resolves correctly in any install. (Previously hard-coded the Owner's\n    # absolute home path, which broke for every other install and tripped the\n    # contamination guard.)\n    project_dir = os.environ.get(\"CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\") or os.getcwd()\n    slug = _rp.project_slug(project_dir)  # PLAN-182 W3 (S321): slug via resolvedor unico, nunca re-derivado\n    mem_dir = Path.home() / \".claude\" / \"projects\" / slug / \"memory\"\n    if not mem_dir.exists():\n        return \"green\", \"memory dir absent\", 0\n    cutoff = time.time() - 30 * 86400\n    n = 0\n    for f in mem_dir.glob(\"*.md\"):\n        try:\n            if f.stat().st_mtime >= cutoff:\n                n += 1\n        except OSError:\n            continue\n    return \"green\", f\"{n} lessons/30d\", n\n","numLines":536,"startLine":1,"totalLines":536}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KTAYFqfYT9mywyEz69aoin","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
