{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UzHnPt6LZBCkkdiA7h4ZU4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tSCOPE OF THIS PAYLOAD\n2\tThis payload is the diff of .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py. Its body is removed, and the file becomes a facade that runs install(globals()) from .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py. install() compiles 10 part files in order and runs them in the facade's own namespace. I judged the facade against the candidate tree: the part files, the installer, the canonical guard list and the tests that read ceo-boot.py.\n3\t\n4\tCHECKED, NO DEFECT\n5\t- How the parts run. They execute in the facade's dictionary (__init__.py:20-26), so:\n6\t  - __file__ is still ceo-boot.py. The lookups based on scripts_dir and parents[2] are unchanged (persona_confidence.py:183,216,275; candidates_lessons.py:202,374).\n7\t  - `global _PLAN_GLOB_CACHE` binds the facade's variable (state_plan_audit.py:6, facade :65).\n8\t  - A monkeypatch on a module attribute reaches the part functions.\n9\t  - TIER_S_CHECKS and TIER_A_CHECKS capture function objects when they are defined, as the monolith did.\n10\t  - check_governance_validate (the only copy) is defined before install(), and the TIER_S_CHECKS list at scheduled_cache.py:311 binds it.\n11\t  - No part defines __all__, deletes names or has a `__name__` guard. main() is only defined in a part and runs from the facade's guard at :187.\n12\t- Moved text. I spot-checked state_plan_audit.py (sanitizer, plan, wait and freshness logic), the spec-drift body in model_persona.py and main() in lessons_cli.py. They match the base text.\n13\t- Python. Standard library only, and compatible with 3.9: the future annotations import is inherited and present in every part, and there is no 3.10-only syntax.\n14\t- Delivery. scripts/install.sh:1520-1550 copies every top-level _lib entry except tests, test_isolation.py and testing.py, so _ceo_boot_parts ships. scripts/upgrade.sh was withheld from the tree, so I could not verify the upgrade path here; the CHANGELOG [1.4.4] says upgrades receive the packages.\n15\t- Fail direction. ceo-boot is a slash-command script, not a registered hook. A missing part fails loudly (ImportError or FileNotFoundError on /ceo-boot) and blocks no session. The advisory checks stay fail-soft.\n16\t- New Tier-S check main_checkout_state (model_persona.py:215, registry entry 25). It is read-only, can only be green or yellow, and turns git timeouts into yellow. It cannot flip gate_pass. It is declared in CHANGELOG [1.4.4] lines 340-341 and 479-480.\n17\t- Protection. The logic moves under the canonical guard `.claude/hooks/_lib/**/*.py` (canonical_edit/guards.py:34), which is stricter than before. It is not on the kernel list, which matches conditions 5 and 7.\n18\t- Conditions. Condition 7 is honest for this file: the logic now lives in modules. Conditions 5, 13 and 14 are not contradicted.\n19\t\n20\tFINDINGS\n21\t\n22\tP2-1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:304 (`_sentinel_patterns`, moved unchanged from the base)\n23\t- Failure: the function reads `_PATTERNS` by AST from .claude/hooks/check_canonical_edit.py. In this delta, PLAN-197 moved `_PATTERNS` to .claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/paths.py:238, and check_canonical_edit.py no longer contains it.\n24\t- Effect: on every /ceo-boot, in this repository and in every install, sentinels_pending_gpg falls back to 4 of the 10 patterns and adds \"[padrões em FALLBACK — a autoridade não foi lida]\" to its summary. It misses only the legacy formats (architect/wave-* grandfathers, staging/review, audit-v2). The check says it is degraded, so the failure is not silent, but the S321 derivation is now dead.\n25\t- Minimal fix: parse .claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/paths.py, or the entry point and then the module. Add a test that asserts derived=True on the real tree.\n26\t\n27\tP2-2 — .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:120-178 (a second copy of check_tier_a_spec_version_drift)\n28\t- Failure: TIER_A_CHECKS (scheduled_cache.py:376) binds the copy at model_persona.py:6, because the registry is built inside install(), before the facade redefines the name at :120. The facade copy is never dispatched.\n29\t- Effect on tests: test_check_vacuous_checks.py `_extract_spec_drift_fn` pulls the facade copy out of ceo-boot.py by AST. The PLAN-178 R2 regression guard now tests dead code: reverting the cure in model_persona.py leaves those tests green.\n30\t- Effect on maintainers: a hand fix in the facade copy changes nothing at runtime. This is the trap condition 7 warns about, inside the facade itself.\n31\t- Honesty: the docstring at :123, \"Lesson validation remains delegated to `_validate_boot_lesson`\", has nothing to do with this function. It exists only so that test_dead_symbol_lesson_render_safe_is_gone (`\"_validate_boot_lesson\" in src`) still passes.\n32\t- Minimal fix: delete the facade copy and the docstring sentence. Have the test take the function from `_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/model_persona.py`, or from `dict(mod.TIER_A_CHECKS)` of the loaded facade.\n33\t\n34\tP2-3 — .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:180-184 and .claude/scripts/check-vacuous-checks.py:133 (checks that read the text of ceo-boot.py now see almost nothing)\n35\t- The vacuous-check lint scans .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py by default. It now sees 2 check_* functions instead of every boot check, including the new main_checkout_state. test_cli_clean_on_real_ceo_boot therefore passes trivially, and its docstring's promise (a new vacuous check turns it red) no longer holds.\n36\t- Two text-presence tests now pass on marker comments, whether or not the registry still wires the check:\n37\t  - test_plan_091_expected_callsites.py:133-146, through `# Tier-S 16th entry: check_tier_policy_misrouting_24h (\"tier_policy_misrouting_24h\")`;\n38\t  - test_ceo_boot_audit_emit.py:93-95, through `# === PLAN-065 Phase 2 audit_emit wire ===`.\n39\t  The facade comment says openly that the markers are there for these checks.\n40\t- Minimal fix: make the lint's default input the facade plus `_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/*.py`. Make the tests load the module and assert registry membership, for example `\"tier_policy_misrouting_24h\" in dict(mod.TIER_S_CHECKS)`. Then drop the markers.\n41\t\n42\tP2-4 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:174-250 (check_hook_live_smoke, moved unchanged)\n43\t- Failure: the check runs py_compile only on the registered entry points. After PLAN-197 those are short facades that compile `_lib/*_parts/*.py` at import; check_bash_safety.py:35-42 is an example.\n44\t- Scenario: an adopter re-applies a hand patch to a part file, as the CHANGELOG asks, and introduces a syntax error, or a part file is missing. The hook crashes at import, `_python-hook.sh` lets the tool call through (an infrastructure fault fails open), and hook_live_smoke still reports green \"N hook(s) smoke-pass\". Before the split, the same broken logic sat in the hook file and showed red as `compile_fail`.\n45\t- This widens a blind spot that already existed: the check never compiled the `_lib` modules that hooks import.\n46\t- Minimal fix: also run py_compile on every file in each facade's `_PARTS` tuple (read by AST), or on every .py under the `_lib` subpackages, and report a missing part as `missing:`.\n47\t\n48\tP2-5 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py:25-26\n49\t- Each part starts with a docstring. When it runs in the facade's dictionary, it overwrites __doc__, so ceo_boot.__doc__ becomes \"Extracted ceo-boot declarations executed by the facade.\". This is cosmetic; argparse uses an explicit description.\n50\t- Minimal fix: save and restore __doc__ around install(), or remove the part docstrings.\n51\t\n52\tP2-6 — stale pointers\n53\t- .claude/hooks/SessionEnd.py:662 (`ceo-boot.py::_validate_boot_lesson`) and docs/threat-model.md:2423 still point at ceo-boot.py. The function now lives at .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/candidates_lessons.py:405.\n54\t- The facade's module docstring (\"15 Tier-S checks\", \"per-check timeout 500 ms\") was already stale in the base and is now 25 checks out of date.\n55\t- Minimal fix: update the references.\n56\t\n57\tNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n58\tNone. No undeclared P1 was found in this payload.\n59\t\n60\tP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n61\tP2-1 through P2-6 above. P2-1 and P2-4 come from moved text whose assumptions PLAN-197 changed: same text, different behavior. P2-2 and P2-3 reduce what this release's test suites prove about ceo-boot, and the CHANGELOG names those suites as the compatibility evidence for the split.\n62\t\n63\tVERDICT: GO No declared condition is false against this payload and there is no P0 or undeclared P1: the ceo-boot facade keeps its runtime behavior, and the six findings are P2 follow-ups (four on narrower test, lint and check coverage, two on stale or misleading text).\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95a0ebeb-18f5-4176-8f95-2931dd13a332","uuid":"971eba5e-5880-49e0-b533-9c90e4d18a98","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:46:39.758Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-26.verdict.txt","content":"SCOPE OF THIS PAYLOAD\nThis payload is the diff of .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py. Its body is removed, and the file becomes a facade that runs install(globals()) from .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py. install() compiles 10 part files in order and runs them in the facade's own namespace. I judged the facade against the candidate tree: the part files, the installer, the canonical guard list and the tests that read ceo-boot.py.\n\nCHECKED, NO DEFECT\n- How the parts run. They execute in the facade's dictionary (__init__.py:20-26), so:\n  - __file__ is still ceo-boot.py. The lookups based on scripts_dir and parents[2] are unchanged (persona_confidence.py:183,216,275; candidates_lessons.py:202,374).\n  - `global _PLAN_GLOB_CACHE` binds the facade's variable (state_plan_audit.py:6, facade :65).\n  - A monkeypatch on a module attribute reaches the part functions.\n  - TIER_S_CHECKS and TIER_A_CHECKS capture function objects when they are defined, as the monolith did.\n  - check_governance_validate (the only copy) is defined before install(), and the TIER_S_CHECKS list at scheduled_cache.py:311 binds it.\n  - No part defines __all__, deletes names or has a `__name__` guard. main() is only defined in a part and runs from the facade's guard at :187.\n- Moved text. I spot-checked state_plan_audit.py (sanitizer, plan, wait and freshness logic), the spec-drift body in model_persona.py and main() in lessons_cli.py. They match the base text.\n- Python. Standard library only, and compatible with 3.9: the future annotations import is inherited and present in every part, and there is no 3.10-only syntax.\n- Delivery. scripts/install.sh:1520-1550 copies every top-level _lib entry except tests, test_isolation.py and testing.py, so _ceo_boot_parts ships. scripts/upgrade.sh was withheld from the tree, so I could not verify the upgrade path here; the CHANGELOG [1.4.4] says upgrades receive the packages.\n- Fail direction. ceo-boot is a slash-command script, not a registered hook. A missing part fails loudly (ImportError or FileNotFoundError on /ceo-boot) and blocks no session. The advisory checks stay fail-soft.\n- New Tier-S check main_checkout_state (model_persona.py:215, registry entry 25). It is read-only, can only be green or yellow, and turns git timeouts into yellow. It cannot flip gate_pass. It is declared in CHANGELOG [1.4.4] lines 340-341 and 479-480.\n- Protection. The logic moves under the canonical guard `.claude/hooks/_lib/**/*.py` (canonical_edit/guards.py:34), which is stricter than before. It is not on the kernel list, which matches conditions 5 and 7.\n- Conditions. Condition 7 is honest for this file: the logic now lives in modules. Conditions 5, 13 and 14 are not contradicted.\n\nFINDINGS\n\nP2-1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:304 (`_sentinel_patterns`, moved unchanged from the base)\n- Failure: the function reads `_PATTERNS` by AST from .claude/hooks/check_canonical_edit.py. In this delta, PLAN-197 moved `_PATTERNS` to .claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/paths.py:238, and check_canonical_edit.py no longer contains it.\n- Effect: on every /ceo-boot, in this repository and in every install, sentinels_pending_gpg falls back to 4 of the 10 patterns and adds \"[padrões em FALLBACK — a autoridade não foi lida]\" to its summary. It misses only the legacy formats (architect/wave-* grandfathers, staging/review, audit-v2). The check says it is degraded, so the failure is not silent, but the S321 derivation is now dead.\n- Minimal fix: parse .claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/paths.py, or the entry point and then the module. Add a test that asserts derived=True on the real tree.\n\nP2-2 — .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:120-178 (a second copy of check_tier_a_spec_version_drift)\n- Failure: TIER_A_CHECKS (scheduled_cache.py:376) binds the copy at model_persona.py:6, because the registry is built inside install(), before the facade redefines the name at :120. The facade copy is never dispatched.\n- Effect on tests: test_check_vacuous_checks.py `_extract_spec_drift_fn` pulls the facade copy out of ceo-boot.py by AST. The PLAN-178 R2 regression guard now tests dead code: reverting the cure in model_persona.py leaves those tests green.\n- Effect on maintainers: a hand fix in the facade copy changes nothing at runtime. This is the trap condition 7 warns about, inside the facade itself.\n- Honesty: the docstring at :123, \"Lesson validation remains delegated to `_validate_boot_lesson`\", has nothing to do with this function. It exists only so that test_dead_symbol_lesson_render_safe_is_gone (`\"_validate_boot_lesson\" in src`) still passes.\n- Minimal fix: delete the facade copy and the docstring sentence. Have the test take the function from `_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/model_persona.py`, or from `dict(mod.TIER_A_CHECKS)` of the loaded facade.\n\nP2-3 — .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:180-184 and .claude/scripts/check-vacuous-checks.py:133 (checks that read the text of ceo-boot.py now see almost nothing)\n- The vacuous-check lint scans .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py by default. It now sees 2 check_* functions instead of every boot check, including the new main_checkout_state. test_cli_clean_on_real_ceo_boot therefore passes trivially, and its docstring's promise (a new vacuous check turns it red) no longer holds.\n- Two text-presence tests now pass on marker comments, whether or not the registry still wires the check:\n  - test_plan_091_expected_callsites.py:133-146, through `# Tier-S 16th entry: check_tier_policy_misrouting_24h (\"tier_policy_misrouting_24h\")`;\n  - test_ceo_boot_audit_emit.py:93-95, through `# === PLAN-065 Phase 2 audit_emit wire ===`.\n  The facade comment says openly that the markers are there for these checks.\n- Minimal fix: make the lint's default input the facade plus `_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/*.py`. Make the tests load the module and assert registry membership, for example `\"tier_policy_misrouting_24h\" in dict(mod.TIER_S_CHECKS)`. Then drop the markers.\n\nP2-4 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:174-250 (check_hook_live_smoke, moved unchanged)\n- Failure: the check runs py_compile only on the registered entry points. After PLAN-197 those are short facades that compile `_lib/*_parts/*.py` at import; check_bash_safety.py:35-42 is an example.\n- Scenario: an adopter re-applies a hand patch to a part file, as the CHANGELOG asks, and introduces a syntax error, or a part file is missing. The hook crashes at import, `_python-hook.sh` lets the tool call through (an infrastructure fault fails open), and hook_live_smoke still reports green \"N hook(s) smoke-pass\". Before the split, the same broken logic sat in the hook file and showed red as `compile_fail`.\n- This widens a blind spot that already existed: the check never compiled the `_lib` modules that hooks import.\n- Minimal fix: also run py_compile on every file in each facade's `_PARTS` tuple (read by AST), or on every .py under the `_lib` subpackages, and report a missing part as `missing:`.\n\nP2-5 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py:25-26\n- Each part starts with a docstring. When it runs in the facade's dictionary, it overwrites __doc__, so ceo_boot.__doc__ becomes \"Extracted ceo-boot declarations executed by the facade.\". This is cosmetic; argparse uses an explicit description.\n- Minimal fix: save and restore __doc__ around install(), or remove the part docstrings.\n\nP2-6 — stale pointers\n- .claude/hooks/SessionEnd.py:662 (`ceo-boot.py::_validate_boot_lesson`) and docs/threat-model.md:2423 still point at ceo-boot.py. The function now lives at .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/candidates_lessons.py:405.\n- The facade's module docstring (\"15 Tier-S checks\", \"per-check timeout 500 ms\") was already stale in the base and is now 25 checks out of date.\n- Minimal fix: update the references.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\nNone. No undeclared P1 was found in this payload.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\nP2-1 through P2-6 above. P2-1 and P2-4 come from moved text whose assumptions PLAN-197 changed: same text, different behavior. P2-2 and P2-3 reduce what this release's test suites prove about ceo-boot, and the CHANGELOG names those suites as the compatibility evidence for the split.\n\nVERDICT: GO No declared condition is false against this payload and there is no P0 or undeclared P1: the ceo-boot facade keeps its runtime behavior, and the six findings are P2 follow-ups (four on narrower test, lint and check coverage, two on stale or misleading text).\n","numLines":64,"startLine":1,"totalLines":64}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UzHnPt6LZBCkkdiA7h4ZU4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
