{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NXswYqZF7kkVU6K2w7EZeC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tPAYLOAD 6/32: nine new files under .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/ (the ceo-boot split, PLAN-197). I also read, from the redacted tree: the facade .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py (its diff is in another payload), the loader _ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py, how install and upgrade enumerate files, and every module the parts load at runtime.\n2\t\n3\tCHECKED, NO FINDING\n4\t- Load order. install() runs the 10 parts in _PARTS order inside the facade's own globals. Every dependency evaluated at load time resolves:\n5\t  - _rp, REPO_ROOT, _PLAN_GLOB_CACHE and check_governance_validate are defined in the facade before install() runs (ceo-boot.py:55-116).\n6\t  - FAILOPEN_RAIL_CLASSIFIERS (liveness_schedule.py) comes after _classify_pair_rail_event (persona_confidence.py).\n7\t  - TIER_S_CHECKS and TIER_A_CHECKS (scheduled_cache.py) come after every check they reference.\n8\t  - _UNSET (candidates_lessons.py) is defined before lessons_cli.py uses it as a default argument.\n9\t- Name binding is unchanged: `global _PLAN_GLOB_CACHE`, `__file__`-relative paths (.claude/scripts for morning_ledger, lessons, persona_demand_* and check-confidence-gate-drift; parents[2] for the repo root), monkeypatch seams, and __module__ all bind to the facade, as before the split.\n10\t- Runtime targets still expose the names the parts call: effective_config, the audit_emit facade (emit_* functions and _KNOWN_ACTIONS), check-model-currency.py, persona_demand_*, check-confidence-gate-drift.py and check_tier_policy_misrouting_24h.py.\n11\t- Delivery: install.sh copies every top-level _lib entry recursively (install.sh:1520-1550). Upgrade enumerates .claude/hooks as a whole (_framework_manifest_set.sh), and _ceo_boot_parts is not excluded.\n12\t- Fail direction: the _wrap_check floor still turns an exception into \"error\". The lesson render gate still drops the lesson when the validator is unavailable (fail-closed). Scheduled-red still never reports green on missing data. No hook runs ceo-boot.py, so a missing part breaks /ceo-boot visibly and never blocks a session.\n13\t- Python: standard library only, and compatible with 3.9.\n14\t- The new main_checkout_state check is read-only and yellow-only, and it never flips gate_pass. CHANGELOG [1.4.4] declares it.\n15\t- Declared conditions: condition 7 holds for ceo-boot (thin facade, path kept). Nothing in this payload makes any of conditions 1-14 false. No P0.\n16\t\n17\tNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n18\t\n19\tP1-a — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:300-325 and :356\n20\t- What it does: _sentinel_patterns() gets the sentinel globs by parsing .claude/hooks/check_canonical_edit.py for a `_PATTERNS =` assignment.\n21\t- What changed: the PLAN-197 split moved that tuple to .claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/paths.py:238. check_canonical_edit.py no longer contains _PATTERNS (grep: no match).\n22\t- Effect: the function always returns (_SENTINEL_PATTERNS_FALLBACK, False), in this repo and in every install.\n23\t- Failure scenario: sentinels_pending_gpg scans 4 of the guard's 10 patterns. It misses the architect/wave-0a, wave-0b, wave-1-2 and wave-minus-1 sentinels, staging/review, and audit-v2. Every /ceo-boot digest ends the row with \"[padrões em FALLBACK — a autoridade não foi lida]\". That brings back the blind guard the S321 cure removed, and a warning that fires on every boot teaches operators to ignore it.\n24\t- Why it matters: this is moved code changing another module's behavior through a source-text dependency (item 4). It contradicts CHANGELOG [1.4.4] \"Entry points keep their paths and their observable contracts\" for this row, and no test covers the derivation on the real tree.\n25\t- Minimal fix: read _lib/canonical_edit/paths.py first and fall back to check_canonical_edit.py. Add a test that _sentinel_patterns() returns derived=True and at least 10 patterns on the real tree.\n26\t\n27\tP1-b — .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:120-184, against _ceo_boot_parts/model_persona.py:6 and scheduled_cache.py:376\n28\t- What it does: the facade defines check_tier_a_spec_version_drift a second time, after install(). TIER_A_CHECKS was built during install() and holds the model_persona.py copy.\n29\t- Effect: --verbose dispatches the part copy, while module.check_tier_a_spec_version_drift is a separate copy that is never dispatched.\n30\t- Text that only satisfies tests:\n31\t  - The facade copy's docstring line \"Lesson validation remains delegated to `_validate_boot_lesson`\" has nothing to do with this function. It satisfies a grep in test_check_vacuous_checks.\n32\t  - The comments at ceo-boot.py:180-184 satisfy text greps in test_plan_091_expected_callsites and test_ceo_boot_audit_emit. The code those tests are about now lives in scheduled_cache.py and telemetry_candidates.py.\n33\t- Failure scenarios:\n34\t  1. Reverting the PLAN-178 C3 cure in model_persona.py (the dispatched copy) leaves the functional regression tests in test_check_vacuous_checks.py green, because they extract the facade copy.\n35\t  2. check-vacuous-checks.py ships with .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py as its default target (line 133). It now sees 2 of the 36 registered check_* functions, so a new always-green check in any part passes the lint and test_cli_clean_on_real_ceo_boot.\n36\t  3. Removing the tier_policy_misrouting_24h registry row from scheduled_cache.py leaves test_plan_091 green, because a comment still names it.\n37\t- Why it matters: this contradicts the facade's own comment (ceo-boot.py:111-113) that monkeypatch seams \"retain their historical identity\". It weakens CHANGELOG [1.4.4] \"The compatibility evidence is the test suites\" for this script (items 4 and 5).\n38\t- Minimal fix:\n39\t  - Delete the facade duplicate and the marker comments.\n40\t  - Point the AST tests and the lint default at _lib/_ceo_boot_parts/*.py plus the facade.\n41\t  - Add an assertion that module.check_tier_a_spec_version_drift is dict(module.TIER_A_CHECKS)[\"tier_a_spec_version_drift\"].\n42\t\n43\tP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n44\t- P2-1 — model_persona.py:241. main_checkout_state treats the default branch as \"main\" when refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is unset (a repo set up with git init + remote add, or with no remote). A repo whose default is master or develop then shows yellow while on its own default branch, but the CHANGELOG says \"off its default branch\". Fix: read init.defaultBranch, or say \"assumed main\" in the summary. Also, three sequential 0.8 s git calls can exceed the 1.0 s soft per-check budget, which has no override. That costs only an annotation.\n45\t- P2-2 — _ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py:25-26. Each part opens with a module docstring, and running the compiled part stores it into the namespace's __doc__. So ceo_boot.__doc__ becomes \"Extracted ceo-boot declarations executed by the facade.\" Fix: drop the part docstrings, or save and restore __doc__ around the loop.\n46\t- P2-3 — ceo-boot logic moved from .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py, which is not a canonical path, to .claude/hooks/_lib/**/*.py, which is canonical (canonical_edit/guards.py:34). Editing ceo-boot checks in an install now needs a sentinel. That tightens governance, but the CHANGELOG does not declare it for ceo-boot.\n47\t- P2-4 — .claude/commands/ceo-boot.md:35 still says \"the 24 Tier-S checks\"; everything else says 25, and the registry asserts 25.\n48\t- P2-5 (carried, not new) — check_hook_live_smoke (harness_governance.py) runs py_compile on every registered hook at each boot, which writes __pycache__/*.pyc next to the adopter's hooks.\n49\t\n50\tVERDICT: GO-WITH-CONDITIONS No declared condition is false against this payload and no P0 was found, but two undeclared P1s must go to the signed annex: after the PLAN-197 split, sentinel-pattern derivation always falls back because it reads a file that no longer holds _PATTERNS, and the facade's never-dispatched spec-drift copy leaves the vacuity lint and its regression tests checking code that /ceo-boot does not run.\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95a0ebeb-18f5-4176-8f95-2931dd13a332","uuid":"d09abbe4-7da8-452e-80a1-ccfdf527769d","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:46:40.772Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-06.verdict.txt","content":"PAYLOAD 6/32: nine new files under .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/ (the ceo-boot split, PLAN-197). I also read, from the redacted tree: the facade .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py (its diff is in another payload), the loader _ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py, how install and upgrade enumerate files, and every module the parts load at runtime.\n\nCHECKED, NO FINDING\n- Load order. install() runs the 10 parts in _PARTS order inside the facade's own globals. Every dependency evaluated at load time resolves:\n  - _rp, REPO_ROOT, _PLAN_GLOB_CACHE and check_governance_validate are defined in the facade before install() runs (ceo-boot.py:55-116).\n  - FAILOPEN_RAIL_CLASSIFIERS (liveness_schedule.py) comes after _classify_pair_rail_event (persona_confidence.py).\n  - TIER_S_CHECKS and TIER_A_CHECKS (scheduled_cache.py) come after every check they reference.\n  - _UNSET (candidates_lessons.py) is defined before lessons_cli.py uses it as a default argument.\n- Name binding is unchanged: `global _PLAN_GLOB_CACHE`, `__file__`-relative paths (.claude/scripts for morning_ledger, lessons, persona_demand_* and check-confidence-gate-drift; parents[2] for the repo root), monkeypatch seams, and __module__ all bind to the facade, as before the split.\n- Runtime targets still expose the names the parts call: effective_config, the audit_emit facade (emit_* functions and _KNOWN_ACTIONS), check-model-currency.py, persona_demand_*, check-confidence-gate-drift.py and check_tier_policy_misrouting_24h.py.\n- Delivery: install.sh copies every top-level _lib entry recursively (install.sh:1520-1550). Upgrade enumerates .claude/hooks as a whole (_framework_manifest_set.sh), and _ceo_boot_parts is not excluded.\n- Fail direction: the _wrap_check floor still turns an exception into \"error\". The lesson render gate still drops the lesson when the validator is unavailable (fail-closed). Scheduled-red still never reports green on missing data. No hook runs ceo-boot.py, so a missing part breaks /ceo-boot visibly and never blocks a session.\n- Python: standard library only, and compatible with 3.9.\n- The new main_checkout_state check is read-only and yellow-only, and it never flips gate_pass. CHANGELOG [1.4.4] declares it.\n- Declared conditions: condition 7 holds for ceo-boot (thin facade, path kept). Nothing in this payload makes any of conditions 1-14 false. No P0.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n\nP1-a — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:300-325 and :356\n- What it does: _sentinel_patterns() gets the sentinel globs by parsing .claude/hooks/check_canonical_edit.py for a `_PATTERNS =` assignment.\n- What changed: the PLAN-197 split moved that tuple to .claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/paths.py:238. check_canonical_edit.py no longer contains _PATTERNS (grep: no match).\n- Effect: the function always returns (_SENTINEL_PATTERNS_FALLBACK, False), in this repo and in every install.\n- Failure scenario: sentinels_pending_gpg scans 4 of the guard's 10 patterns. It misses the architect/wave-0a, wave-0b, wave-1-2 and wave-minus-1 sentinels, staging/review, and audit-v2. Every /ceo-boot digest ends the row with \"[padrões em FALLBACK — a autoridade não foi lida]\". That brings back the blind guard the S321 cure removed, and a warning that fires on every boot teaches operators to ignore it.\n- Why it matters: this is moved code changing another module's behavior through a source-text dependency (item 4). It contradicts CHANGELOG [1.4.4] \"Entry points keep their paths and their observable contracts\" for this row, and no test covers the derivation on the real tree.\n- Minimal fix: read _lib/canonical_edit/paths.py first and fall back to check_canonical_edit.py. Add a test that _sentinel_patterns() returns derived=True and at least 10 patterns on the real tree.\n\nP1-b — .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:120-184, against _ceo_boot_parts/model_persona.py:6 and scheduled_cache.py:376\n- What it does: the facade defines check_tier_a_spec_version_drift a second time, after install(). TIER_A_CHECKS was built during install() and holds the model_persona.py copy.\n- Effect: --verbose dispatches the part copy, while module.check_tier_a_spec_version_drift is a separate copy that is never dispatched.\n- Text that only satisfies tests:\n  - The facade copy's docstring line \"Lesson validation remains delegated to `_validate_boot_lesson`\" has nothing to do with this function. It satisfies a grep in test_check_vacuous_checks.\n  - The comments at ceo-boot.py:180-184 satisfy text greps in test_plan_091_expected_callsites and test_ceo_boot_audit_emit. The code those tests are about now lives in scheduled_cache.py and telemetry_candidates.py.\n- Failure scenarios:\n  1. Reverting the PLAN-178 C3 cure in model_persona.py (the dispatched copy) leaves the functional regression tests in test_check_vacuous_checks.py green, because they extract the facade copy.\n  2. check-vacuous-checks.py ships with .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py as its default target (line 133). It now sees 2 of the 36 registered check_* functions, so a new always-green check in any part passes the lint and test_cli_clean_on_real_ceo_boot.\n  3. Removing the tier_policy_misrouting_24h registry row from scheduled_cache.py leaves test_plan_091 green, because a comment still names it.\n- Why it matters: this contradicts the facade's own comment (ceo-boot.py:111-113) that monkeypatch seams \"retain their historical identity\". It weakens CHANGELOG [1.4.4] \"The compatibility evidence is the test suites\" for this script (items 4 and 5).\n- Minimal fix:\n  - Delete the facade duplicate and the marker comments.\n  - Point the AST tests and the lint default at _lib/_ceo_boot_parts/*.py plus the facade.\n  - Add an assertion that module.check_tier_a_spec_version_drift is dict(module.TIER_A_CHECKS)[\"tier_a_spec_version_drift\"].\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n- P2-1 — model_persona.py:241. main_checkout_state treats the default branch as \"main\" when refs/remotes/origin/HEAD is unset (a repo set up with git init + remote add, or with no remote). A repo whose default is master or develop then shows yellow while on its own default branch, but the CHANGELOG says \"off its default branch\". Fix: read init.defaultBranch, or say \"assumed main\" in the summary. Also, three sequential 0.8 s git calls can exceed the 1.0 s soft per-check budget, which has no override. That costs only an annotation.\n- P2-2 — _ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py:25-26. Each part opens with a module docstring, and running the compiled part stores it into the namespace's __doc__. So ceo_boot.__doc__ becomes \"Extracted ceo-boot declarations executed by the facade.\" Fix: drop the part docstrings, or save and restore __doc__ around the loop.\n- P2-3 — ceo-boot logic moved from .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py, which is not a canonical path, to .claude/hooks/_lib/**/*.py, which is canonical (canonical_edit/guards.py:34). Editing ceo-boot checks in an install now needs a sentinel. That tightens governance, but the CHANGELOG does not declare it for ceo-boot.\n- P2-4 — .claude/commands/ceo-boot.md:35 still says \"the 24 Tier-S checks\"; everything else says 25, and the registry asserts 25.\n- P2-5 (carried, not new) — check_hook_live_smoke (harness_governance.py) runs py_compile on every registered hook at each boot, which writes __pycache__/*.pyc next to the adopter's hooks.\n\nVERDICT: GO-WITH-CONDITIONS No declared condition is false against this payload and no P0 was found, but two undeclared P1s must go to the signed annex: after the PLAN-197 split, sentinel-pattern derivation always falls back because it reads a file that no longer holds _PATTERNS, and the facade's never-dispatched spec-drift copy leaves the vacuity lint and its regression tests checking code that /ceo-boot does not run.\n","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NXswYqZF7kkVU6K2w7EZeC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
