{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BUa8zbYfSKe43E4Xbzemop","type":"tool_result","content":"70\tresult under the project runtime state dir (resolved by the single resolver\n71\t``_lib/runtime_paths.py``); every later offline run reads that cache and\n72\treports its age. Executables run: ``claude --version`` (one code-defined\n73\t``[<bin>, \"--version\"]`` probe; skipped by ``--no-probe``; from ``$PATH`` or\n74\t``--claude-bin``, never from a file) and, ONLY under ``--fetch``, that one\n75\t``npm view`` (from ``$PATH`` or ``--npm-bin``). ``codex`` is never run.\n76\t\n77\tThe re-pin recommendation first asks ``re-pin-codex.py`` (``mold_inventory``)\n78\twhether a pack already pins the version: then the next step is to apply that\n79\tpack (the Owner's ceremony), never to generate another. Otherwise it asks\n80\t``newest_mold`` which mold the generator would build from, so it never names\n81\ta mold the generator refuses; for a constants-block mold the command carries\n82\t``--ga-tag``. When the newest pack's mold is not generator-compatible it says\n83\t\"clone it by hand\" and names why.\n84\t\n85\tAdopter shape of the catalog check: without ADR-149 the comparison is NOT\n86\tAPPLICABLE and the Claude Code binary is not scanned at all. This file ships\n87\tto adopters (``install.sh`` copies every ``.claude/scripts/*.py``); in an\n88\tadopter tree the three comparisons report NOT APPLICABLE (no pin manifest,\n89\tthe ledger is the maintainer's, no ADR-149) — see \"Adopter shape\" above.\n90\t\n91\tWiring: when this file was introduced nothing ran it — not ``/ceo-boot``\n92\t(``.claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py``), not a workflow, not the release\n93\tpreflight — and ``re-pin-codex.py`` is reached only through the commands\n94\tthis script prints. Until a caller exists, the latency it cures (a new model\n95\tor a codex release noticed days late) stays uncured: it answers only when\n96\tsomeone runs it. The natural caller is ``/ceo-boot``, offline (no\n97\t``--fetch``), reading the cache an explicit ``--fetch`` left.\n98\t\n99\tExit codes:\n100\t  0 — always in report mode (drift, unknown and infra failures included)\n101\t  1 — ``--strict`` only: at least one ``drift`` finding\n102\t  2 — CLI usage error (argparse)\n103\t\n104\tEmits NO audit events. Apart from the bytecode the Python interpreter itself\n105\tcaches for the standard library at startup, it writes nothing except the\n106\t``--fetch`` cache file: the repo modules it loads at run time write no\n107\tbytecode, and npm's own cache, logs and\n108\tupdate-notifier state are pointed at a throwaway directory next to the cache\n109\tfile and removed when the fetch returns. Probe output is untrusted: it is\n110\tparsed against a strict grammar and never echoed (a failed probe reports its\n111\trc only); scraped display names keep only a plain-name charset.\n112\tStdlib only. Python >= 3.9.\n113\t\"\"\"\n114\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n115\t\n116\timport argparse\n117\timport datetime as _dt\n118\timport hashlib\n119\timport importlib.util"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95a0ebeb-18f5-4176-8f95-2931dd13a332","uuid":"f48c5ac5-f9df-4ee1-845d-3fd0ed75fccf","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:47:28.919Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/scripts/check-substrate-drift.py","content":"result under the project runtime state dir (resolved by the single resolver\n``_lib/runtime_paths.py``); every later offline run reads that cache and\nreports its age. Executables run: ``claude --version`` (one code-defined\n``[<bin>, \"--version\"]`` probe; skipped by ``--no-probe``; from ``$PATH`` or\n``--claude-bin``, never from a file) and, ONLY under ``--fetch``, that one\n``npm view`` (from ``$PATH`` or ``--npm-bin``). ``codex`` is never run.\n\nThe re-pin recommendation first asks ``re-pin-codex.py`` (``mold_inventory``)\nwhether a pack already pins the version: then the next step is to apply that\npack (the Owner's ceremony), never to generate another. Otherwise it asks\n``newest_mold`` which mold the generator would build from, so it never names\na mold the generator refuses; for a constants-block mold the command carries\n``--ga-tag``. When the newest pack's mold is not generator-compatible it says\n\"clone it by hand\" and names why.\n\nAdopter shape of the catalog check: without ADR-149 the comparison is NOT\nAPPLICABLE and the Claude Code binary is not scanned at all. This file ships\nto adopters (``install.sh`` copies every ``.claude/scripts/*.py``); in an\nadopter tree the three comparisons report NOT APPLICABLE (no pin manifest,\nthe ledger is the maintainer's, no ADR-149) — see \"Adopter shape\" above.\n\nWiring: when this file was introduced nothing ran it — not ``/ceo-boot``\n(``.claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py``), not a workflow, not the release\npreflight — and ``re-pin-codex.py`` is reached only through the commands\nthis script prints. Until a caller exists, the latency it cures (a new model\nor a codex release noticed days late) stays uncured: it answers only when\nsomeone runs it. The natural caller is ``/ceo-boot``, offline (no\n``--fetch``), reading the cache an explicit ``--fetch`` left.\n\nExit codes:\n  0 — always in report mode (drift, unknown and infra failures included)\n  1 — ``--strict`` only: at least one ``drift`` finding\n  2 — CLI usage error (argparse)\n\nEmits NO audit events. Apart from the bytecode the Python interpreter itself\ncaches for the standard library at startup, it writes nothing except the\n``--fetch`` cache file: the repo modules it loads at run time write no\nbytecode, and npm's own cache, logs and\nupdate-notifier state are pointed at a throwaway directory next to the cache\nfile and removed when the fetch returns. Probe output is untrusted: it is\nparsed against a strict grammar and never echoed (a failed probe reports its\nrc only); scraped display names keep only a plain-name charset.\nStdlib only. Python >= 3.9.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport datetime as _dt\nimport hashlib\nimport importlib.util","numLines":50,"startLine":70,"totalLines":1285}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BUa8zbYfSKe43E4Xbzemop","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
